# -- NEVER PUSH --------------------------------------------
_private/
DangerDoNotHoldInMemory/
data/raw/
*.vault
*.enc
.env
venv/
.venv/

# -- WIP folders (uncomment to push when proven) -----------
# NOTE the shape: `lens/*`, not `lens/`. Excluding the DIRECTORY makes git stop
# at it and never descend, so a later `!lens/whatever` would silently do nothing.
# Excluding the CONTENTS instead lets a negation below actually re-include one.
lens/*
#
# ...except alien_tk. Three sims that were sitting loose in CoolAlienTech/,
# outside that stale clone, in no git anywhere. The folder is being deleted, so
# lens/ discipline ("no public push until proven") would have made this disk the
# single copy of files nobody has a second of. Received work gets tracked; it
# does not get promoted to shell/ or IO_PAGES until it is actually proven.
!lens/alien_tk/

