# -- CURSE 31: Helena builds are LOCAL/PRIVATE; git keeps only the MIRROR --------
# The pattern (level 12, snappy pushes): the heavy build DATA never enters git.
# It lives on your disk (private). Git tracks only the tiny MIRROR -- MANIFEST.json
# + build_card.json per version -- so another mage sees the exact steps and can
# regenerate the whole net locally. "Pay thea Heleni in compute."
#   novice:  py -3 pipe.py --max 9 --k 4 --bits 10101      (rebuild from scratch)
#   advanced: py -3 redundancy.py repair builds/vNNN/net    (rebuild csv from bin+zip)
builder/helena_net/builds/**
# ...but KEEP the mirror (the steps, not the payload).
# Re-include every DIRECTORY so git can descend, then re-include only the mirror files:
!builder/helena_net/builds/**/
!builder/helena_net/builds/**/MANIFEST.json
!builder/helena_net/builds/**/build_card.json
!builder/helena_net/builds/**/BROKEN.txt

# -- Private scrolls (cave walls) ----------------------
*_PRIVATE.md
*.mp3
# ...but slimium_toon.mp3 is NOT a private scroll. It is a live dependency:
# shell/fslimium_v1.0.html does `new Audio('slimium_toon.mp3')` and both serve
# 200 on Pages. The blanket rule above over-reached onto a deliberate public
# asset, so it sat ignored-but-tracked -- a file the repo needs and its own
# rules disown. Evicting it would have killed the audio on a live page in
# silence (found 2026-09-05, L197).
!shell/slimium_toon.mp3

Cchats/
# kibotos build artifacts (regenerated by golden_stack_tmm.py)
kibotos/*.svg
kibotos/__pycache__/

kibotos/**/__pycache__/

# -- CURSE 32: the TITANS are vendored, never re-pushed --------------------------
# SpEngLab/_titans holds shallow clones of other people's public repos,
# read as inspiration for the hardware lane. Two clones = 130 MB (Slow-Silicon
# ships ~60 MB of real die trace/geometry .bin; text-to-cad carries LFS + a
# 4.5 MB sourcemap). That is the 100 MB wall in a single `git add .`.
# We keep their FILES on disk (private, local) and their IDEAS in our own scrolls.
# Their licences are quoted in SpEngLab/TITANS.md -- credit lives in git,
# payload does not. Nested .git dirs would become gitlinks here anyway.
SpEngLab/_titans/

# -- GRAPHIUM node cache (mirror, not payload -- same rule as helena_net) -------
# graphium.py defaults to workdir="./.graphium" and memoises every node to disk
# by content hash. Those .json files are REGENERABLE: the demo runs on
# Provider.echo(), so re-running reproduces them byte for byte. The receipt is
# NOT -- it records wall clock, measured speedup and the Amdahl p of one real
# run on one real machine. Ignore what a rerun can rebuild; keep the measurement.
#
# VERIFIED, not assumed (2026-09-01): ran `graphium.py --demo` in a clean temp
# dir and compared. 26/26 cache files identical by sha256. The receipt was not:
#   old  0.23s  5.49x  p=0.82        new  0.35s  4.34x  p=0.77
# Same critical path (scope -> audit -> check -> report), different machine
# moment. That is exactly the line between payload and measurement.
Gos/ponderTheOrb/.graphium/**
!Gos/ponderTheOrb/.graphium/**/
!Gos/ponderTheOrb/.graphium/**/receipt_*.txt
